<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.KOREA KOCOPIA BUYS 105,000 TONNES OF U.S. CORN.</title>
<headline>S.KOREA KOCOPIA BUYS 105,000 TONNES OF U.S. CORN.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Corn Processing Industry Association (KOCOPIA) bought 105,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 corn from Cargill on Friday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The U.S. giant grain company has an option to choose the corn shipment from between the Pacific Northwest or the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Details of the tenders are: POSITION  TONNES  SHIPMENT</p>
<p>	     PRICE ONE	 52,500  Nov. 5-25 (PNW)</p>
<p>$133.54</p>
<p>			Oct.20-Nov.10 (Gulf)     $132.74 TWO</p>
<p>52,500  Nov. 20-Dec.10 (PNW)     $133.78</p>
<p>			Nov. 5-25 (Gulf)	   $132.98</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5650</p>
